  "title": "Erdős Problem #336",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "For $r\\geq 2$ let $h(r)$ be the maximal finite $k$ such that there exists a basis $A\\subseteq \\mathbb{N}$ of order $r$ (so every large integer is the sum of at most $r$ integers from $A$) and exact order $k$ (so every large integer is the sum of exactly $k$ integers from $A$).\nFind the value of $ \\lim_r \\frac{h(r)}{r^2}. $ ",
